==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-opt|pt}} {{term|tomar|lang=roa-opt}}, of {{unk.|pt|title=unknown}} origin. Possibly derived from {{etyl|la|pt}} {{term|autumo|autumāre|I reckon; I affirm|lang=la}}<ref>Yakov Malkiel, ''Etymology''</ref>.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Portugal}} {{IPA|/tuˈmaɾ/|lang=pt}}
* {{audio|Pt tomar.ogg|Audio|lang=pt}}
* {{homophones|Tomar|lang=pt}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb|tom|ar}}

# {{lb|pt|transitive}} to {{l|en|take}} {{gloss|to get something into one’s possession or control}}
#: {{ux|pt|Fui ao banco '''tomar''' meu dinheiro.|I went to the bank to '''get''' my money.}}
## {{lb|pt|transitive|military}} to {{l|en|take}}; to {{l|en|conquer}} {{gloss|to seize control of a location}}
##: {{ux|pt|Os cruzados '''tomaram''' Jerusalém.|The crusaders '''took''' Jerusalem.}}
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} to {{l|en|steal}} {{gloss|to take something illegally}}
##: {{ux|pt|O ladrão '''tomou''' todo o meu dinheiro.|The thief '''has taken''' all my money.}}
# {{lb|pt|transitive}} to {{l|en|take}}; to {{l|en|receive}} {{gloss|to be the victim of an interaction}}
#: {{ux|pt|'''Tomei''' um soco na cara.|'''I took''' a punch to the face.}}
# {{lb|pt|transitive|applicable to some nouns}} to put into practice
#: {{ux|pt|'''tomar''' uma decisão|to make a decision}}
#: {{ux|pt|'''tomar''' medidas|to take measures}}
# {{indtr|pt|por|ditr=1}} to {{l|en|take for}}; to {{l|en|consider}}; to {{l|en|regard}} {{gloss|to have a certain opinion about someone or something}}
#: {{ux|pt|Eu '''tomei''' a Maria por corrupta.|I '''took''' Mary for a corrupt.}}
# {{lb|pt|transitive}} to take into the body
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} to {{l|en|drink}} {{gloss|to ingest a liquid}}
##: {{ux|pt|Eu '''tomei''' suco.|I '''drank''' juice.}}
## {{lb|pt|intransitive|by extension}} to {{l|en|drink}} {{gloss|to consume alcoholic beverages, especially habitually}}
##: {{ux|pt|Ele '''toma''' muito, durante os finais de semana.|He '''drinks''' a lot on weekends.}}
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} to {{l|en|take}} {{gloss|to use a medicine}}
##: {{ux|pt|Esqueci de '''tomar''' meus antidepressivos.|I forgot to '''take''' my antidepressants.}}

